# The assessment of AGT-005 against this build. The requirement identifier is this
# file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the identity
# is a second place for it to be wrong -- the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a record
# registration, and CHK-003.assessment states for this registry.
#
# AGT-005: "KnowledgeWorkbench shall supply provenance-preserving claims, decisions,
# contradictions, and context; Nomos shall supply deterministic findings and observations."
# One clause per product.
#
# The KWB clause is genuinely KWB's own build and outside this workspace, per
# ARC-ECOSYSTEM-001's ownership table ("Why was a design chosen? KWB. What did a source or a
# decision claim? KWB."), so this verdict assesses only the Nomos clause.
#
# 'Findings' is well satisfied: `Finding` (rule, subject identity, `EvidenceClass`,
# `Applicability`, `GateCategory`) is exactly a deterministic judgment, real and tested,
# produced by every `nomos gate run` through `Handle_Gate_Run`. `EvidenceClass::Observed`
# even names "directly observed at runtime" as one of `Finding`'s own evidence classes.
#
# 'Observations', in this requirement's own section (agent-and-knowledgeworkbench
# integration), is really pointing at the harness run-history crossing ARC-ECOSYSTEM-001's
# third diagram draws (a run's own observations becoming a KWB lesson) -- and
# ARC-HARNESS-001 states outright that crossing is unbuilt: its own table marks "Run
# history" unbuilt and its closing section says plainly nothing here is built. `RunId`
# identifies one execution today but nothing persists a run's outcome across runs as a
# queryable observation.
verdict: Partial
